  "review": {
    "summary": "The curated subset is strongly fail-closed and generally consistent, with bounded artifact handling, explicit execution approvals, conservative scanner triage, and structured V1\u2013V6 verification. Three medium contract gaps remain: an incomplete #4b detector, an overbroad generation prohibition on legitimate attachment assertions, and an underspecified V6 summary row.",
    "scores": {
      "semantic_correctness": 92,
      "false_positive_control": 95,
      "security_trust_boundaries": 96,
      "verification_design": 89,
      "scope_contract_consistency": 91,
      "docs_usability": 94
    },
    "findings": [
      {
        "severity": "M",
        "category": "verification_design",
        "file": "skills/e2e-reviewer/scripts/scan.sh",
        "line": 5042,
        "title": "Parameterized toBeAttached assertions evade #4b scanning",
        "evidence": "The #4b Tier 3 expression matches only the exact empty-argument form `toBeAttached()`, although the documented pattern covers positive `toBeAttached` assertions generally. Valid forms such as `toBeAttached({ timeout: 5000 })` receive no mechanical candidate, and #4b is absent from the mandatory fallback token sweep.",
        "recommendation": "Match a positive `toBeAttached(` call with arbitrary bounded arguments, retain the existing negative-form exclusion, and leave contextual severity confirmation to Phase 2."
      },
      {
        "severity": "M",
        "category": "semantic_correctness",
        "file": "skills/playwright-test-generator/code-rules.md",
        "line": 156,
        "title": "Generation rule rejects a documented legitimate attachment contract",
        "evidence": "The forbidden-pattern table directs `toBeAttached()` to `toBeVisible()` and exempts only negative and dynamically injected cases. The authoritative pattern contract also recognizes attachment as meaningful when a CSS-hidden element must remain in the DOM, so generation guidance can replace a semantically correct assertion with a different visibility contract.",
        "recommendation": "Permit `toBeAttached()` whenever DOM attachment itself is the approved outcome, including CSS-hidden persistence, and forbid it only when attachment is weak evidence for a visibility or removal promise."
      },
      {
        "severity": "M",
        "category": "scope_contract_consistency",
        "file": "skills/e2e-reviewer/references/verification-rules.md",
        "line": 15,
        "title": "Condensed V6 proof omits fresh-context separation",
        "evidence": "The cross-framework proof table describes V6 as rerunning `e2e-reviewer` after repair, while the generator contract requires a distinct fresh-context, read-only reviewer and explicitly rejects inline self-review as PASS. The condensed row can therefore be followed without the separation needed for a valid V6 verdict.",
        "recommendation": "Change the V6 proof cells to require rerunning `e2e-reviewer` in a distinct fresh-context, read-only actor or process that did not write or repair the candidate."
      }
    ],
